    description: "FOUND 2026-10-25 (premise check of META-sigap), fixture only.\n\n`class Local; def initialize; end; end` and, in the SAME file, `Local.new` -> the call resolves to ruby:Local:0-0:initialize:external_symbol (unresolved) although Local and its initialize are defined in that file. Ruby construction calls go through `.new`, which the analyzer emits as a plain calls edge to an external placeholder instead of an instantiates edge to the in-repo class (or a calls edge to its initialize).\n\nExpected: an in-repo `Local.new` binds to the in-repo Local (instantiates, matching java/cs/php/ts in-repo `new Local()`), and its initialize is reachable. Distinct from WI-jubag (EXTERNAL constructors) and INV-dosoz (nested-namespace registration). Not measured on a corpus."  # 4371
